  "status_text": "One circuit can test every allowance for lights going out with no gates that flip bits. Lean checked this for dots linked exactly when their subtrees of one tree overlap. A light must be on when its dot and neighbors are unchosen and off when its dot is chosen. For any selected set and k from 0 to n, the circuit says whether every fit whose lights only fall exceeds the largest independent set size by more than k drops on some subset. With n dots and t tree nodes, it uses at most 12(n+1)^2(t+1)(t+n^3+1) AND/OR gates reading at most two wires, with two free constants (L-meta-48151).",
